A||||2||jelly2m8||Hangin' with skitime||||1||
Z||000000||jelly2m8||08-12-2001||03:07 PM|||| As those of you who know, skitime is traveling through the maritime provinces.<P> We have had the pleasure of spending yesterday with David and Vonnie. They arrived here late Friday night, and left early this morning. We set them up in our back yard instead of finding them a campground.<P> Yesterday morning we attended a fairly small local car show, Dav&Von drove one of our cars there. After the show we spent the afternoon checking out some of the local sites, and dinner.<P> I sent Dav&Von out in the V8 when we returned home,and told him to drive it as his own. Although he couldnt get much for clear roads, and the car still needs decent wheels/tires & brakes, I could hear that David wasn't scared to push the pedal to the floor! Hopefully next time he gets a chance to drive it, I will have the car the way it should be.<P> We spent last evening drinking beer, and playing card games with some local friends of mine. All through our all to short encounter I had interesting conversations with them, with David willing to tell all on his mods to his car. I can't wait to see their rides. <P> I was able to show them several local Fiero's, although none, mine included can match in the condition of theirs. Maybe skitime and friends can hook me up with the parts I want to whip my cars back to attention.<P> David and Vonnie are amazing people, as some of you already know. The GF and I are very happy to have had the chance to get to know them. We talked about Fieros, friends, our pasts, etc. All of which was really great. There was never a dull moment with Dave & Vonnie around.<P> Hopefully next summer we will get a chance to visit skitime and friends in their area, they speak very highly of their friends and acquaintances (sp?) local, and those on the forum. The GF and I have already talked about next summers vacation.<P> We helped Dav&Von to pick out some scenic spots along their route of travel, and gave Wade Custance of Truro a call so that he would be home, so that they can check out his "Lethal Weapon".<P> Early this morning, we said our pleasentries and good-byes, Hopefully we'll get the chance to meet again soon. <P>Anthony Cook<BR>aka: jelly2m8<BR> <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||08-13-2001||10:28 AM||||Hey Anthony, the pleasure was all ours. Thank you for the hospitallity.  If anyone needs a unbelievably talented Fiero mechanic in Eastern Canada, he is the man.  He does work on them which would be impossible by most.  Anthony and Lori made us feel at home and we had fun with Tim and Leslie too. Tim had the most rusted Fiero I had ever seen but Anthony will be fixing it too. <BR> <BR>PS - We found two Fieros in a yard in Novia Scotia. The notchback bodies are complete and one has a good areo nose too. One cradle and a good dash for Lori's car. Neither car was wrecked. Maybe some unrusted metal for Tim's car too. We will give details later because I don't want others to get to it first. He said less than $800 for the two complete cars too. <P>Might be heading to Prince Edward Island today.||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||08-18-2001||12:38 AM||||Anthony, We made it home safely tonight.  Tomorrow is the Fiero Dutch Classic show near us so we will be taking our cars to the show.  Hope you found those cars in the junkyard. ||||reg||1
